     Definition 0.3.5 (Open and closed intervals of R).

    Let a, b P R such that a ă b. We name the subset of all numbers between a and b
     in different ways depending on whether or not the ends of the interval (a and b)
    are elements of the subset.

     • The closed interval [a, b] = tx P R  : a ď x ď bu — both end points are
          included.

     • The open interval (a, b) = tx P R  : a ă x ă bu — neither end point is
          included.

