2.2 Ĳ Definition of the Derivative

   We now define the “derivative” explicitly, based on the limiting slope ideas of the previous
    section. Then we see how to compute some simple derivatives.
       Let us now generalise what we did in the last section so as to find “the slope of the
    curve y =  f (x) at (x0, y0)” for any smooth enough4 function f (x).
     As before, let (x0, y0) be any point on the curve y =  f (x). So we must have y0 =  f (x0).
  Now let (x1, y1) be any other point on the same curve. So y1 =  f (x1) and x1 ‰ x0. Think


