                                                            f x0 + ∆x ´ f (x0)
                              lim
                           ∆xÑ0      ∆x



When we talk of the “slope of the curve” at a point, what we really mean is the slope of
the tangent line to the curve at that point. So “the slope of the curve y =  f (x) at (x0, y0)”
is also the limit7 expressed in the above equation. The derivative of f (x) at x = x0 is also
defined to be this limit. Which leads8 us to the most important definition in this text:





