APPLICATIONS OF DERIVATIVES                                       3.2 RELATED RATES


  • The statement of the problem will tell you quantities that must be related (above it
    was volume, radius and, implicitly, time).

  • Typically a little geometry (or some physics or...)  will allow you to relate these
      quantities (above it was the formula that links the volume of a sphere to its radius).

  • Implicit differentiation will then allow you to link the rate of change of one quantity
      to another.

   Another balloon example

