3.6.3 §§ Second Derivative — Concavity

    The second derivative f 2(x) tells us the rate at which the derivative changes. Perhaps the
      easiest way to understand how to interpret the sign of the second derivative is to think
     about what it implies about the slope of the tangent line to the graph of the function.
     Consider the following sketches of y = 1 + x2 and y = ´1 ´ x2.





      • In the case of y =  f (x) = 1 + x2 ,  f 2(x) = 2 ą 0. Notice that this means the slope,
