                                 lim   = DNE
                               xÑa g(x)

and if F = 0 but G ‰ 0 then
                                                                   f (x)
                                  lim   = 0
                                 xÑa g(x)

However when both F, G = 0 then, as we saw in Example 1.4.6, almost anything can
happen

