                                  lim   =                                 xÑa g(x)    g1(a),

     (b) while, if  f 1(x) and g1(x) exist, with g1(x) nonzero, on an open interval that
        contains a, except possibly at a itself, and if the limit

                                                      f 1(x)
                           lim       exists or is +8 or is ´8
                          xÑa g1(x)

       then

                                                                f (x)            f 1(x)
                                lim   = lim
                               xÑa g(x)   xÑa g1(x)



Proof. We only give the proof for part (a). The proof of part (b) is not very difficult, but
uses the Generalised Mean–Value Theorem (Theorem 3.4.38), which is optional and most
readers have not seen it.

