has to be P = 420(1 + r)´n. That is what is meant by the statement “The present value6 of
a $420 payment made n months in the future, when the interest rate is 100r% per month,
compounded monthly, is 420(1 + r)´n.”
  Now back to the original problem. We will be making 60 monthly payments of $420.
