      The advantage that the secant method has over Newton’s method is that it does not
    use the derivative of f. This can be a substantial advantage, for example when evaluation
     of the derivative is computationally difficult or expensive. On the other hand, the above
    example suggests that the secant method is not as fast as Newton’s method. The following
     section shows that this is indeed the case.

