 Example 2.1.5 (Escape Velocity)

Suppose that you shoot a probe straight up from the surface of the Earth — at what initial
speed must the probe move in order to escape Earth’s gravity?

Solution.  We determine this by computing how much work must be done in order to
escape Earth’s gravity. If we assume that all of this work comes from the probe’s initial
kinetic energy, then we can establish the minimum initial velocity required.


