2.2Ĳ Averages

   Another frequent12 application of integration is computing averages and other statistical
    quantities. We will not spend too much time on this topic — that is best left to a proper
    course in statistics — however, we will demonstrate the application of integration to the
   problem of computing averages.
       Let us start with the definition13 of the average of a finite set of numbers.




