3.3.6 §§ Convergence Test List

   We now have half a dozen convergence tests:

      • Divergence Test

            – works well when the nth term in the series fails to converge to zero as n tends to
                 infinity

      • Alternating Series Test

            – works well when successive terms in the series alternate in sign

            – don’t forget to check that successive terms decrease in magnitude and tend to
               zero as n tends to infinity

      • Integral Test

            – works well when, if you substitute x for n in the nth term you get a function,
