  • The step size here, as in the preliminary version, is chosen so that the local truncation
                                                                      |A1,n+1´A2,n+1|     Kh2/2    K                                            =                                                                                                  h, is                                                                                          h                                                                                                  2      error in A2,n+1 per unit increase of t, namely r =        h    «
     approximately ε. So h is roughly proportional to ε.

  • On the other hand, (E7) shows that, in the full method, local truncation error is being
                                   O(h3)
    added to yn+1 at a rate of   h = O(h2) per unit increase in t.

  • So one would expect that local truncation increases the error at a rate proportional
      to ε2 per unit increase in t.

  • If the rate of increase of error were exactly a constant time ε2, then the error accu-
     mulated between the initial time t = 0 and the final time t = t f would be exactly a
     constant times ε2 t f .

  • However we have seen that, once some local truncation error has been introduced,
       its contribution to the global error can grow exponentially with t f . So we would
                                                                                actual error at t=t f
     expect that, under the full Euler/Euler-2step method,                 to be more or                                                                                                   ε2t f
      less independent of ε, but still growing exponentially in t f .

