D.3.4 §§ The Kutta-Merson Process

     The Kutta-Merson process28 uses two variations of the Runge-Kutta method. Each step
      involves five calculations29 of f:

                                  k1,n =  f (tn, yn)
                                  k2,n =  f  tn + 13h, yn + 3hk1,n1
                                  k3,n =  f  tn + 13h, yn + 6hk1,n1   + 16hk2,n
                                  k4,n =  f  tn + 12h, yn + 8hk1,n1   + 38hk3,n
                                  k5,n =  f  tn + h, yn + 2hk1,n1   ´ 32hk3,n + 2hk4,n
     Once these five evaluations have been made, the process generates two approximations
       for y(tn + h):
                                             h                  i
                               A1,n+1 = yn + h
                                             h                                                        2k1,n1  ´ 32k3,n + 2k4,n i
                               A2,n+1 = yn + h  6k1,n1  + 3k4,n2  + 16k5,n

