                                                         Example 1.2.22


  We now move on to learning about the properties of the cross product. Our first prop-
erties lead up to a more intuitive geometric definition of a ˆ b, which is better for inter-
preting a ˆ b. These properties of the cross product, which state that a ˆ b is a vector and
