    In the event that dx and dy are both nonzero, we can rewrite this as


                                           Equation 1.3.2 (Symmetric Equation).

                                    x ´ x0 = y ´ y0
                                          dx       dy



   which is called the symmetric equation for the line.
    A second way to specify a line in two dimensions is to give one point (x0, y0) on the
    line and one vector n =  nx, ny  whose direction is perpendicular to that of the line.  If

