Observe that the coefficients nx, ny of x and y in the equation of the line are the compo-
nents of a vector  nx, ny  perpendicular to the line. This enables us to read off a vector
perpendicular to any given line directly from the equation of the line. Such a vector is
called a normal vector for the line.

