     Definition 2.1.3 (Continuity).

    Let
       ˝ m and n be natural numbers
       ˝ a P Rm
       ˝ the function f (x) be defined for all x near a and take values in Rn

     (a) The function f is continuous at a point a if

                                   lim f (x) =  f (a)
                                 xÑa

     (b) The function f is continuous on a set D if it is continuous at every point of D.



