in the sketch, is tangent to our surface.
    Similarly, to minimize x + y + 3z, imagine slowly decreasing the value of C. As we do
so, the plane x + y + 3z = C moves to the left. We want to stop decreasing C at the smallest
value of C for which the plane x + y + 3z = C intersects our surface x2 + 2y2 + 3z2 = 72.
For that value of C the plane x + y + 3z = C, which is represented by the left hand blue
line in the sketch, is again tangent to our surface. The previous Example 2.5.10 was similar,
except that the plane was z = C.
