      use the following variant of Theorem 2.10.2.

         Theorem 2.10.8 (Two Lagrange Multipliers).

           Let f (x, y, z), g(x, y, z) and h(x, y, z) have continuous first partial derivatives in a
           region of R3 that contains the curve C given by the equations

                                        g(x, y, z) = h(x, y, z) = 0

