Solution.  Before leaping into integration, we should try to understand what the surface
and volume look like. For each constant z0, the part of the surface z = 1 ´ 3x2 ´ 2y2 that
lies in the horizontal plane z = z0 is the ellipse 3x2 + 2y2 = 1 ´ z0. The biggest of theseellipses is that in the xy-plane, where z0 = 0. It is the ellipse 3x2 + 2y2 = 1. As z0 increases
the ellipse shrinks, degenerating to a single point, namely (0, 0, 1), when z0 = 1. So the
surface consists of a stack of ellipses and our solid is
