Consequently

  •  if m is even, then f (x, y) is even under x Ñ ´x and
  •  if m is odd, then f (x, y) is odd under x Ñ ´x and
  •  if n is even, then f (x, y) is even under y Ñ ´y and
  •  if n is odd, then f (x, y) is odd under y Ñ ´y and

  •  if m + n is even, then f (x, y) is even (under reflection across the origin) and

  •  if m + n is odd, then f (x, y) is odd (under reflection across the origin).


