    complications by exploiting the fact that, by symmetry, the total mass of the sphere will
   be eight times the mass in the first octant. We shall cut the first octant part of the sphere
    into tiny pieces using Cartesian coordinates. That is, we shall cut it up using planes of
    constant z, planes of constant y, and planes of constant x, which we recall look like


