3.7.1 §§ Spherical Coordinates

     In the event that we wish to compute, for example, the mass of an object that is invariant
    under rotations about the origin, it is advantageous to use another generalization of polar
     coordinates to three dimensions. The coordinate system is called spherical coordinates.


          Definition 3.7.1.

          Spherical coordinates are denoted37 ρ, θ and φ and are defined by

             ρ = the distance from (0, 0, 0) to (x, y, z)
           φ = the angle between the z axis and the line joining (x, y, z) to (0, 0, 0)
              θ = the angle between the x axis and the line joining (x, y, 0) to (0, 0, 0)


