 Example 1.0.4  Parametrization of ey = 1 + x2

A very easy method that can often create parametrizations for a curve is to use x or
y as a parameter. Because we can solve ey = 1 + x2 for y as a function of x, namely
y = ln 1 + x2  , we can use x as the parameter simply by setting t = x. This gives the
parametrization
                            r(t) =  t , ln(1 + t2)    ´ 8 ă t ă 8

