 Example 1.0.5  Parametrization of x2 + y2 = a2, again

It is also quite common that one can use either x or y to parametrize part of, but not all of,
a curve. A simple example is the circle x2 + y2 = a2. For each ´a ă x ă a, there are two
points on the circle with that value of x. So one cannot use x to parametrize the whole
circle. Similarly, for each ´a ă y ă a, there are two points on the circle with that value of
y. So one cannot use y to parametrize the whole circle. On the other hand
