2.2Ĳ Optional — Field Lines

   Suppose that we drop a tiny stick into a river8 with the velocity field of the flowing water
    being v(x, y). We are assuming, for simplicity, that the velocity field does not depend9 on
    time t. The stick will move along with the water10. When the stick is at r, its velocity will
   be the same as the velocity of the water at r, which is v(r). Thus if the stick is at r(t) at
    time t, we will have
                                     dr
                         = v r(t)
                                       dt

   The stick will trace out a path, parametrized by r(t).


