2.4Ĳ Line Integrals

   We have already seen, in §1.6, one type of integral along curves. We are now going to see
    a second, that turns out to have significant connections to conservative vector fields.  It
    arose from the concept of “work” in classical mechanics.
      Suppose that we wish to find the work done by a force F(r) moving a particle along
    a path r(t). During the “infinitesimal time interval23” from t to t + dt the particle moves
   from r(t) to r(t) + dr with dr = drdt(t) dt. By definition, the work done during that in-
    finitesimal time interval is

                                                 dr
                          F r(t)   ¨ dr = F r(t)   ¨ dt(t) dt

   The total work done during the time interval from t0 to t1 is then

