4.1Ĳ Gradient, Divergence and Curl


    “Gradient, divergence and curl”, commonly called “grad, div and curl”, refer to a very
    widely used family of differential operators and related notations that we’ll get to shortly.
   We will later see that each has a “physical” significance. But even if they were only short-
    hand1, they would be worth using.
       For example, one of Maxwell’s equations (relating the electric field E and the magnetic
     field B) written without the use of this notation is

