                  ψ is any function, then        if B = ∇ˆ A), and if
              ∇ˆ (A + ∇ψ) = ∇ˆ A + ∇ˆ ∇ψ = B
    by the vector identity Theorem 4.1.7.b. That is, A + ∇ψ is another vector potential for B.
