§§§ An Application of the Heat Equation

As an application, we look at the temperature a short distance below the surface of the
Earth. For simplicity, we make the Earth flat29 and we assume that the temperature, T,
depends only on time, t, and the vertical coordinate, z. Then the heat equation simplifies
to
                          BT (z, t) = αB2T (z, t)                        (HE)
