4.7Ĳ Optional — A Generalized Stokes’ Theorem

   As we have seen, the fundamental theorem of calculus, the divergence theorem, Greens’
   theorem and Stokes’ theorem share a number of common features. There is in fact a single
   framework which encompasses and generalizes all of them, and there is a single theorem
    of which they are all special cases. We now give a bare bones introduction to this frame-
   work and theorem. A proper treatment typically takes up a good part of a full course.
   Here is an outline of what we shall do:


