2.7.2  Computing a Basis for a Subspace



Now we show how to ﬁnd bases for the column space of a matrix and the null
space of a matrix. In order to ﬁnd a basis for a given subspace, it is usually best
to rewrite the subspace as a column space or a null space ﬁrst: see this important
note in Section 2.6.





A basis for the column space   First we show how to compute a basis for the
column space of a matrix.





Theorem. The pivot columns of a matrix A form a basis for Col(A).





Proof. This is a restatement of a theorem in Section 2.5.



