3.4.2  Matrix multiplication

In this subsection, we introduce a seemingly unrelated operation on matrices,
namely, matrix multiplication. As we will see in the next subsection, matrix multi-
plication exactly corresponds to the composition of the corresponding linear trans-
formations. First we need some terminology.

Notation. Let A be an m × n matrix. We will generally write ai j for the entry in
the ith row and the jth column. It is called the i, j entry of the matrix.



