Theorem. Let A be an n × n matrix, and let (A | In ) be the matrix obtained by
augmenting A by the identity matrix. If the reduced row echelon form of (A | In ) has
the form ( In | B ), then A is invertible and B = A−1. Otherwise, A is not invertible.



