subset
           P =  a1x1 + a2x2 + ··· + anxn  0 ≤a1, a2,..., an ≤1  .

   In other words, a parallelepiped is the set of all linear combinations of n vectors
with coefﬁcients in [0,1]. We can draw parallelepipeds using the parallelogram
law for vector addition.

