Remark (Multiplicativity of |det|). The above theorem also gives a geometric
reason for multiplicativity of the (absolute value of the) determinant. Indeed, let
A and B be n × n matrices, and let T, U : Rn →Rn be the corresponding matrix
transformations. If C is the unit cube, then

            vol T ◦U(C) = vol T(U(C)) = |det(A)|vol(U(C))
                        = |det(A)| · |det(B)|vol(C)
                        = |det(A)| · |det(B)|.

On the other hand, the matrix for the composition T ◦U is the product AB, so

                  vol T ◦U(C) = |det(AB)|vol(C) = |det(AB)|.

Thus |det(AB)| = |det(A)| · |det(B)|.



