                        α    ∥x∥


   In particular, α = 90◦if and only if cos(α) = 0, which happens if and only if
∥y −x∥2 = ∥x∥2 + ∥y∥2. Therefore,

      x and y are perpendicular ⇐⇒∥x∥2 + ∥y∥2 = ∥y −x∥2
                ⇐⇒x · x + y · y = (y −x) · (y −x)
                ⇐⇒x · x + y · y = y · y + x · x −2x · y
                ⇐⇒x · y = 0.

To reiterate:

         x ⊥y  ⇐⇒   x · y = 0  ⇐⇒   ∥y −x∥2 = ∥x∥2 + ∥y∥2.



