                 P [           X P(Ai) − X X P(Ai ∩Aj) + · · · + (−1)n−1P __OPEN_BOOK_BACKSLASH__ Ai              (4.6)                             Ai                                                                                                                                                                                i=1       = i=1           i=1 j=i+1                                                                                                                                                                                                       i=1                     

   6. The Theorem of Total Probability. Let B1, B2, ..., Bn be mutually exclusive and exhaustive. Then

