which means that given the information that a Head has occurred, we no longer need to account for the
outcome TT, and the remaining three outcomes are equally likely with exactly two outcomes lying in the set
B.

Example 4.30 (Rolling a die twice.). Toss a six-sided die twice. The sample space consists of all ordered
