Example 5.7. Roll 12 dice simultaneously, and let X denote the number of 6’s that appear. We wish to
ﬁnd the probability of getting seven, eight, or nine 6’s. If we let S = {get a 6 on one roll}, then P(S ) = 1/6
and the rolls constitute Bernoulli trials; thus X ∼binom(size = 12, prob = 1/6) and our task is to ﬁnd
P(7 ≤X ≤9). This is just
