Again, one method to solve this problem would be to generate a probability mass table and add up the
relevant rows. However, an alternative method is to notice that P(7 ≤X ≤9) = P(X ≤9) −P(X ≤6) =
FX(9) −FX(6), so we could get the same answer by using the Binomial tail probabilities... menu
in the R Commander or the following from the command line:

> pbinom(9, size=12, prob=1/6) - pbinom(6, size=12, prob=1/6)

[1] 0.001291758

