5.5  The Empirical Distribution

Do an experiment n times and observe n values x1, x2, ..., xn of a random variable X. For simplicity in most
of the discussion that follows it will be convenient to imagine that the observed values are distinct, but the
remarks are valid even when the observed values are repeated.

