is said to have Student’s t distribution with r degrees of freedom, and we write X ∼t(df = r). The associated
R functions are dt,pt, qt, and rt, which give the PDF, CDF, quantile function, and simulate random variates,
respectively. See Section 8.2.


Snedecor’s F distribution

A random variable X with PDF

                          Γ[(m + n)/2] m m/2       m   −(m+n)/2
