How to do it with R

There are not any speciﬁc functions in the prob package [116] designed for multivariate expectation. This is
not a problem, though, because it is easy enough to do expectation the long way – with column operations.
We just need to keep the deﬁnition in mind. For instance, we may compute the covariance of (U, V) from
Example 7.5.

> Eu <- sum(S$U*S$probs)
> Ev <- sum(S$V*S$probs)
> Euv <- sum(S$U*S$V*S$probs)
> Euv - Eu * Ev



