we use a scatterplot matrix which is made with the splom function in the lattice package [182] as shown
below. The plot is shown in Figure 12.1.
   The dependent (response) variable Volume is listed in the ﬁrst row of the scatterplot matrix. Moving from
left to right, we see an approximately linear relationship between Volume and the independent (explanatory)
variables Height and Girth. A ﬁrst guess at a model for these data might be

                              Y = β0 + β1x1 + β2x2 + ϵ,                                   (12.7)

in which case the quantity µ(x1, x2) = β0 + β1x1 + β2x2 would represent the mean value of Y at the point
(x1, x2).



