Remark 12.2. The formula in Equation (12.13) is convenient for mathematical study but is inconvenient for
numerical computation. Researchers have devised much more eﬃcient algorithms for the actual calculation
of the parameter estimates, and we do not explore them here.

Remark 12.3. We have only found a critical value, and have not actually shown that the critical value is a
minimum. We omit the details and refer the interested reader to [172].


How to do it with R

We do all of the above just as we would in simple linear regression. The powerhouse is the lm function.
Everything else is based on it. We separate explanatory variables in the model formula by a plus sign.

> trees.lm <- lm(Volume ~ Girth + Height, data = trees)
> trees.lm

