   The syntax for general prediction does not change much from simple linear regression. The computations
are done with the predict function as described below.
   The only diﬀerence from SLR is in the way we tell R the values of the explanatory variables for which we
want predictions. In SLR we had only one independent variable but in MLR we have many (for the trees
data we have two). We will store values for the independent variables in the data frame new, which has two
columns (one for each independent variable) and three rows (we shall make predictions at three diﬀerent
locations).

> new <- data.frame(Girth = c(9.1, 11.6, 12.5),
