the Intercept is signiﬁcant in the aforementioned model.

   3In other words, a variable might be highly signiﬁcant one moment but then fail to be signiﬁcant when another variable is added to
the model. When this happens it often indicates a problem with the explanatory variables, such as multicollinearity. See Section 12.7.3.



