Remark 12.6. When a model includes a quadratic term for an independent variable, it is customary to also
include the linear term in the model. The principle is called parsimony. More generally, if the researcher
decides to include xm as a term in the model, then (s)he should also include all lower order terms x, x2,
...,xm−1 in the model.

  We do estimation/prediction the same way that we did in Section 12.2.2, except we do not need a Height
column in the dataframe new since the variable is not included in the quadratic model.

