Example 13.1 (Eﬀectiveness of Insect Sprays). The InsectSprays data records counts of insects treated
with insecticides labeled "A" through "F". In Exercise ?? the reader is asked to check the normality of count
by spray, and .


How to do it with R

We perform a test that the location parameters are all the same with the kruskal.test function. The p-value
returned is based on the asymptotic chi-squared distribution.

> kruskal.test(count ~ spray, data = InsectSprays)

        Kruskal-Wallis rank sum test

data:  count by spray
Kruskal-Wallis chi-squared = 54.691, df = 5,
p-value = 1.511e-10

   Here we reject the null hypothesis that all treatment eﬀects are the same.

