15.5  Odds and Odds Ratios

15.5.1  Odds of an event

Odds in favor of A is
                                                        P(A)
                           Odds in favor of event A =                                     (15.21)                                                   1 −P(A).

15.5.2  Odds ratio

Here we have an underlying model that looks like this:

                                          Success  Failure  Total
                            Group 1     π11       π12     π1+
                                                                                                 (15.22)
                            Group 2     π21       π22     π2+
                                     Total      π+1      π+2     1

The odds ratio associated with this model is

                                             π11/π12    π11π22
                            ψ =      =            ,                                  (15.23)
                                             π21/π22    π21π12

and it represents the odds in favor of success for Group 1 divided by the odds in favor of success for Group
2. We observe a sample and construct a sample contingency table which we write like this:

                                          Success  Failure  Total
                            Group 1     n11       n12     n1+
                                                                                                 (15.24)
                            Group 2     n21       n22     n2+
                                     Total      n+1      n+2     n



