  No problems there, and here is a graphical display.

> fourfold(x)

   The graph looks good. We go on to perform the CMH test.

> mantelhaen.test(x)



15.6. COHRAN-MANTEL-HAENSZEL (CMH) TEST STATISTIC                            327


        Mantel-Haenszel chi-squared test with continuity
        correction

data:  x
Mantel-Haenszel X-squared = 5.8073, df = 1,
p-value = 0.01596
alternative hypothesis: true common odds ratio is not equal to 1
95 percent confidence interval:
 0.3982316 0.8966439
sample estimates:
common odds ratio
        0.5975549

   The marginal odds ratio of Sex versus Age is signiﬁcantly diﬀerent from one (the common odds ratio is
estimated to be approximately 0.597554932729288). We estimate the odds of being a male child at approxi-
mately half the odds of being a female child, consistently across social status.



