E.5.3  Positive (Semi)Deﬁnite

If the matrix A satisﬁes xTAx ≥0 for all vectors x , 0, then we say that A is positive semideﬁnite.  If
strict inequality holds for all x , 0, then A is positive deﬁnite. The connection to statistics is that covariance
matrices (see Chapter 7) are always positive semideﬁnite, and many of them are even positive deﬁnite.

