We use the following rules to decide whether (a, b) is an extremum (that is, a local minimum or local maxi-
mum) of f.

                                ∂2 f
   •  If det(H) > 0 and ∂x2 (a, b) > 0, then (a, b) is a local minimum of f.

                                ∂2 f
   •  If det(H) > 0 and ∂x2 (a, b) < 0, then (a, b) is a local maximum of f.

   •  If det(H) < 0, then (a, b) is a saddle point of f and so is not an extremum of f.

   •  If det(H) = 0, then we do not know the status of (a, b); it might be an extremum or it might not be.

