      zero.
  b. When your car is moving at constant velocity down the street, the net force must also be zero according to
     Newton’s first law. The car’s frictional force between the road and tires opposes the drag force on the car with
     the same magnitude, producing a net force of zero. The body continues in its state of constant velocity until
