         As with most problems, we next need to identify what needs to be determined and what is known or can be inferred
         from the problem as stated, that is, make a list of knowns and unknowns. It is particularly crucial to identify the
         system of interest, since Newton’s second law involves only external forces. We can then determine which forces
          are external and which are internal, a necessary step to employ Newton’s second law. (See Figure 6.2(c).) Newton’s
           third law may be used to identify whether forces are exerted between components of a system (internal) or between



