          Although gravity is the weakest of the four fundamental forces of nature, its attractive nature is what holds us to
           Earth, causes the planets to orbit the Sun and the Sun to orbit our galaxy, and binds galaxies into clusters, ranging
         from a few to millions. Gravity is the force that forms the Universe.


