        An indicator called the Reynolds number    can reveal whether flow is laminar or turbulent. For flow in a tube of
          uniform diameter, the Reynolds number is defined as

                                                                                                     14.20


         where   is the fluid density, v its speed,   its viscosity, and r the tube radius. The Reynolds number is a
