        Some musical instruments, such as woodwinds, brass, and pipe organs, can be modeled as tubes with symmetrical
         boundary conditions, that is, either open at both ends or closed at both ends (Figure 17.24). Other instruments can
         be modeled as tubes with anti-symmetrical boundary conditions, such as a tube with one end open and the other
