The Doppler effect and the Doppler shift have many important applications in science and engineering. For example,
the Doppler shift in ultrasound can be used to measure blood velocity, and police use the Doppler shift in radar (a
microwave) to measure car velocities. In meteorology, the Doppler shift is used to track the motion of storm clouds;
