to be macroscopic, that is, to consist of a huge number (such as       ) of molecules. Then we can say that a system
is in thermal equilibrium with itself if all parts of it are at the same temperature. (We will return to the definition of a
thermodynamic system in the chapter on the first law of thermodynamics.)
1.2 Thermometers and Temperature Scales

LEARNING OBJECTIVES
By the end of this section, you will be able to:
