Thermal Expansion in Two and Three Dimensions

Unconstrained objects expand in all dimensions, as illustrated in Figure 1.7. That is, their areas and volumes, as well
as their lengths, increase with temperature. Because the proportions stay the same, holes and container volumes
also get larger with temperature. If you cut a hole in a metal plate, the remaining material will expand exactly as it
would if the piece you removed were still in place. The piece would get bigger, so the hole must get bigger too.

