         conducted quasi-statically. An isothermal line on a (p, V) diagram is represented by a curved line from starting point
     A to finishing point B, as seen in Figure 3.10. For an ideal gas, an isothermal process is hyperbolic, since for an ideal
         gas at constant temperature,            .





