The magnitude of the electric force  on one of the charges is proportional to the magnitude of its own charge and
the magnitude of the other charge, and is inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them:



This proportionality becomes an equality with the introduction of a proportionality constant. For reasons that will
become clear in a later chapter, the proportionality constant that we use is actually a collection of constants. (We
discuss this constant shortly.)

