Area Vector

For discussing the flux of a vector field, it is helpful to introduce an area vector    This allows us to write the last
equation in a more compact form. What should the magnitude of the area vector be? What should the direction of
the area vector be? What are the implications of how you answer the previous question?

The area vector of a flat surface of area A has the following magnitude and direction:

    •  Magnitude is equal to area (A)
    •  Direction is along the normal to the surface (  ); that is, perpendicular to the surface.

Since the normal to a flat surface can point in either direction from the surface, the direction of the area vector of an
