       The Electric Field at the Surface of a Conductor

             If the electric field had a component parallel to the surface of a conductor, free charges on the surface would move,
         a situation contrary to the assumption of electrostatic equilibrium. Therefore, the electric field is always
          perpendicular to the surface of a conductor.

