There is no magnetic force on static charges. However, there is a magnetic force on charges moving at an angle to a
magnetic field. When charges are stationary, their electric fields do not affect magnets. However, when charges
move, they produce magnetic fields that exert forces on other magnets. When there is relative motion, a connection
between electric and magnetic forces emerges—each affects the other.

