Significance
The cross product in this formula results in a third vector that must be perpendicular to the other two. Other
physical quantities, such as angular momentum, also have three vectors that are related by the cross product. Note
that typical force values in magnetic force problems are much larger than the gravitational force. Therefore, for an
isolated charge, the magnetic force is the dominant force governing the charge’s motion.


