         The last property is related to the fact that the north and south poles cannot be separated. It is a distinct difference
         from electric field lines, which generally begin on positive charges and end on negative charges or at infinity. If
           isolated magnetic charges (referred to as magnetic monopoles) existed, then magnetic field lines would begin and
         end on them.





