The microwaves in a microwave oven reflect off the walls of the oven, so that the superposition of waves produces
standing waves, similar to the standing waves of a vibrating guitar or violin string (see Normal Modes of a Standing
Sound Wave (http://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-1/pages/17-4-normal-modes-of-a-standing-
sound-wave)). A rotating fan acts as a stirrer by reflecting the microwaves in different directions, and food
turntables, help spread out the hot spots.

