Working on the same principle as these optical reflectors, corner reflectors are routinely used as radar reflectors
(Figure 1.11) for radio-frequency applications. Under most circumstances, small boats made of fiberglass or wood
do not strongly reflect radio waves emitted by radar systems. To make these boats visible to radar (to avoid
collisions, for example), radar reflectors are attached to boats, usually in high places.





