         FIGURE 1.42 (a) Polarized light is rotated    by a liquid crystal and then passed by a polarizing filter that has its axis perpendicular to the
            direction of the original polarization. (b) When a voltage is applied to the liquid crystal, the polarized light is not rotated and is blocked by
           the filter, making the region dark in comparison with its surroundings. (c) LCDs can be made color specific, small, and fast enough to use in
