           tip of the arrow. The figure shows three rays from many rays that emanate from the tip of the arrow. These three
         rays can be traced by using the ray-tracing rules given above.

              •  Ray 1 enters the lens parallel to the optical axis and passes through the focal point on the opposite side (rule
                 1).
              •  Ray 2 passes through the center of the lens and is not deviated (rule 2).
              •  Ray 3 passes through the focal point on its way to the lens and exits the lens parallel to the optical axis (rule



