radiation of a much longer wavelength and its diffraction limit was significantly poorer than Hubble’s. The Arecibo telescope was still very
useful, because important information is carried by radio waves that is not carried by visible light. It collapsed in 2020 and there are
currently no plans to rebuild it. (credit: Jeff Hitchcock)


