          PROBLEM-SOLVING STRATEGY

         Relativity
             1. Make a list of what is given or can be inferred from the problem as stated (identify the knowns). Look in
                 particular for information on relative velocity v.
             2.  Identify exactly what needs to be determined in the problem (identify the unknowns).
             3. Make certain you understand the conceptual aspects of the problem before making any calculations (express
