        do not use a rounded number in a subsequent calculation. Also, check the answer to see if it is reasonable: Does it
        make sense? This may be more difficult for relativity, which has few everyday examples to provide experience with
         what is reasonable. But you can look for velocities greater than c or relativistic effects that are in the wrong direction
          (such as a time contraction where a dilation was expected).

