(absorption), or it can give away energy to the radiation in the cavity (emission). The absorption process sends the
oscillator to a higher quantum state, and the emission process sends the oscillator to a lower quantum state.
Whichever way this exchange of energy goes, the smallest amount of energy that can be exchanged is hf. There is no
upper limit to how much energy can be exchanged, but whatever is exchanged must be an integer multiple of hf. If
the energy packet does not have this exact amount, it is neither absorbed nor emitted at the wall of the blackbody.
