When Planck first published his result, the hypothesis of energy quanta was not taken seriously by the physics
community because it did not follow from any established physics theory at that time. It was perceived, even by
Planck himself, as a useful mathematical trick that led to a good theoretical “fit” to the experimental curve. This
perception was changed in 1905 when Einstein published his explanation of the photoelectric effect, in which he
gave Planck’s energy quantum a new meaning: that of a particle of light.
