In this section, we consider the effects of electron spin. Spin introduces two additional quantum numbers to our
model of the hydrogen atom. Both were discovered by looking at the fine structure of atomic spectra. Spin is a
fundamental characteristic of all particles, not just electrons, and is analogous to the intrinsic spin of extended
bodies about their own axes, such as the daily rotation of Earth.

