PET scans are especially useful to examine the brain’s anatomy and function. For example, PET scans can be used to
monitor the brain’s use of oxygen and water, identify regions of decreased metabolism (linked to Alzheimer’s
disease), and locate different parts of the brain responsible for sight, speech, and fine motor activity

