   Assumptions and Stereotypes

   Du Bois experiences the veil between worlds as a Black American because of assumptions and stereotypes.
    Unfortunately, such assumptions and stereotypes still exist in America today. In Chapter 2, you have begun to
    learn about the impact of language on culture and about how developing anti-racist and inclusive ideas is an
    important part of the composition process.

   Read the following scenario.

   Mark is an assistant manager at a neighborhood convenience store. At the end of the evening, his inventory
    count is short. After an examination of the store, Mark notices that a large display of novelty items is nearly
    empty. Knowing his store sells only a few of those items each day, Mark identifies theft of the items as the likely
    source of the discrepancy. He thinks back through the customers he served that day.
