INTRODUCTION “Literacy is now understood as a means of . . . communication in an increasingly digital, text-
mediated, information-rich, and fast-changing world,” according to UNESCO. The literacy narrative is a genre
that provides an account of an individual or a member of a community and their experience with learning.
