INTRODUCTION This chapter explores the process of profile writing. Writers compose these articles or
essays to present some essential insight about the subject to the audience; subjects can span a wide variety of
topics, including individuals, groups, places, and events. A good profile tells one clear, overarching story,
chosen from other possible stories about the subject.
