5.6 Editing Focus: Verb Tense Consistency

LEARNING OUTCOMES

By the end of this section, you will be able to:
  •  Apply various editing strategies to a draft in progress.
  •  Implement consistent use of verbs in a draft in progress.

When you edit, you make changes at the sentence level: phrasing, grammar, mechanics, and wording. Read
your paper aloud to check for needed editing. Alternately, you could have your device read the paper to you if it
has that feature. As you read or listen, if you notice that something does not sound quite right, your draft
probably needs editing at that point. Additionally, if your electronic draft shows blue underlining, check
whether you should accept the changes suggested by your software. Once you have thoroughly reviewed each
sentence in your draft, read aloud or listen to the entire piece again to see how it flows, making any additional
