    LEARNING OUTCOMES

    By the end of this section, you will be able to:
        •  Describe technical writing as a career path.
        •  Explore the field of technical writing in greater depth.

       If you like science and technical fields and you like to write, you may want to explore technical writing as a
     career path. Technical writers usually have a degree in English, journalism, or communication. Often, they
     also have knowledge, college coursework, or a degree in a specialized field such as computer science,
     engineering, medicine, biology, agriculture, and other technical fields, such as manufacturing, construction,
     welding, and plumbing; however, companies will usually train technical writers on the subject needed and the
