         Although mythological and thus fictional, the movie features many references to African American history and
         the African American experience: slavery and the slave trade, colonization, the exploitation of Africa, civil rights,
         Black militancy, systemic poverty, and the loss of Black men—especially fathers—to violence and incarceration.
        These topics are usually whitewashed or ignored in popular cinema because of their graphic and racially
         charged nature.

