         Drafting: Thesis Statement, Analysis, and Supporting Examples

     After you have selected a topic and decided on the evaluation criteria, spend some time looking closely at your
    primary source (the film, TV show, book, etc. you have chosen to review). With these criteria in mind, view/
     read/listen to your primary source. Take notes on how your selected evaluation criteria apply to your source.
    When you come across strong and relevant examples, write down vivid, detailed descriptions of the scene and
     quote applicable dialogue. By looking closely at your primary source and taking notes now, you will have solid
    and specific examples to illustrate your points later when you draft your review.

