Drafting the Body

For the body of the review, provide more background and context wherever you think such information is
necessary. Because the purpose of this part of the review is to present the main points that support the thesis,
be sure to show how these points explain the criteria on which you have based your evaluation. Back up the
main points with specific, concrete evidence from your primary source. At this point, return to your early notes
and use the descriptions and quotations you gathered. You will likely have collected more evidence as well. Use
a graphic organizer like Table 7.6 to create your draft. Main points 1 and 2 should be your topic sentences.
