         Although his book identifies unstable housing as a cause of poverty, Desmond writes for the purpose of creating
        empathy in voters and establishing facts that policy makers cannot ignore to remedy the housing trap. The
        moving description of eviction and its effects allows readers to fully appreciate his proposed solutions. As a
