    Desmond relays the stories of Kamala and others to generate empathy with readers. These stories create
    emotional appeal in that they allow readers to experience the spiraling effects of poverty along with people
    they come to care about. Indeed, Desmond relies on the intensity of Kamala’s story to give poverty a face.
    Kamala is no longer a nameless, faceless statistic. She is a real woman who experiences the loss of a child as a
     result of circumstances beyond her control. Kamala’s story helps break the preconception that poor people are
     lazy and make individual choices to perpetuate their own poverty. Her situation illustrates a cycle of
    unbreakable tragedy and poverty that begins with her inability to secure affordable and stable housing. The
     details of her story make it hard for the public to ignore.

