Language in Law

In the legal world, communication is equally or even more crucial. In addition to the ability to speak
convincingly, the ability to use rhetorical strategies to write persuasively is of critical importance in legal
professions and in everyday situations regarding disputes, contracts, and other matters involving legalities. In
courtrooms and behind the scenes, the ability to persuade a judge to make a decision or ruling in favor of a
particular client before or during a trial affects all aspects of a case, including the legal team’s ability to
persuade a jury of its position. Furthermore, disputes between family members, buyers and sellers, renters
and landlords, and employees and managers are often settled with the help of appropriately used rhetorical
strategies.
