    deaths occur mainly in low- and middle-income countries where, in stark contrast, the rate of childhood obesity
      is rising. Globally, 1.9 billion adults and 38.3 million children are overweight or obese (“Obesity”).
     Undernutrition and obesity can be found in the same household, largely a result of eating energy-dense foods
     that are high in fat and sugars. The global impact of malnutrition, which includes both undernutrition and
