Language and Expression

One significant finding of Broca’s case study was that Leborgne grew up in the town of Moret-sur-Loing. The
town had many tanneries, leading Broca to theorize that Leborgne’s use of the syllable tan was related to his
home. Whyisthistheoryimportant? It illustrates how personal history affects people. It is possible that
Leborgne used language in this way because of his history and cultural association with his hometown. Culture
and identity have a big impact on how people use language, even among people who speak the same language.





