    or-no question or one with an obvious answer.
  •  Debatable. The research question should spark reasonable debate around the best answer or solution. If
    you think you know the answer to the research question or if you doubt that people can be open-minded
    about a range of answers, it is not a good research question.
  •  Answerable. You should be able to answer your research question by using the evidence you gather. You
    should be able to consult existing source material on the topic.
  •  Consequential. The outcome of the debate around your research question should be of consequence. In
    other words, what you or others choose to do going forward should matter and affect others.

