Homographs

Homographs have the same spelling but different meanings. They are considered different from homonyms
because they may be pronounced differently. Some disagreement exists among scholars as to whether
pronunciation must be different for a word to be considered a homograph. Some experts insist that origins
must differ as well. However, all agree that meanings differ. For more information about homographs, see
Words and Language.

Here are some common homographs and their meanings:


