INTRODUCTION Many people spend a substantial portion of their time watching and assessing
images—including photographs, memes, graphs, and videos—via television, streaming services, and social
media platforms. Even the college curriculum is as much visual as it is verbal, including as it does Internet
research, computer graphics, and PowerPoint presentations. These forms of media might be relatively new,
but people have been creating and consuming images for millennia, as you can see in Figure 17.1. An
important part of human development consists of making images, enjoying them, and talking about them.

Formerly, visual texts were created exclusively by painters, photographers, and others generally designated as
