rock concert featuring the band Naked Raygun with several concertgoers in the foreground. Such pictures are
common forms of memorabilia that serve an archival function. The features common to visual rhetoric—point
of view, arrangement, color, and symbol—do not inspire much in the way of discussion in this particular image.
Parts are blurry, some of the figures are obscure, and the picture’s purpose is unclear. Therefore, any analysis
of the image may be guided more by personal opinion than by critical thinking. Such images are not the focus
of this chapter.





