    Media and Other Visuals

     Because speeches are auditory by nature, you can enhance their effectiveness by using media and other visual
      aids. These elements can add emphasis, help the audience understand a complex idea, or otherwise support
     your message. But be careful not to detract from your speech with the media you choose. A common error
     speakers make is to include too much or irrelevant media.





