  MLA Paper Format

     Follow your instructor’s formatting guidelines or those indicated here. For sample papers with MLA format and
     works-cited pages, visit this site (https://openstax.org/r/this-site1).

        •  Margins. Use one-inch margins on all sides.
        •  Spacing. Double-space throughout the paper, including the works-cited page.
        •  Paragraph format. Indent paragraphs one-half inch.
        •  Page numbers. Start numbering on the first page of your paper and continue to the end of the works-cited
         page. Place page numbers in the upper-right corner, and add your last name before the page number:
        “Coleman 3.”



