On the other end of the intelligence spectrum are those individuals whose IQs fall into the highest ranges.
Consistent with the bell curve, about 2% of the population falls into this category. People are considered to
have a higher aptitude for learning (and may be classified as "gifted" within educational systems) if they have
an IQ score of 130 or higher, or superior intelligence in a particular area. Long ago, popular belief suggested
that people of high intelligence were maladjusted. This idea was disproven through a groundbreaking study of
