 Prader-Willi Syndrome
  Prader-Willi Syndrome (PWS) is a genetic disorder that results in persistent feelings of intense hunger and
 reduced rates of metabolism. Typically, affected children have to be supervised around the clock to ensure that
 they do not engage in excessive eating. Currently, PWS is the leading genetic cause of severe obesity in children,
 and it is associated with a number of cognitive deficits and emotional problems (Figure 10.12).
