inventories. It asks a series of true/false questions that are designed to provide a clinical profile of an
individual. Projective tests use ambiguous images or other ambiguous stimuli to assess an individual’s
unconscious fears, desires, and challenges. The Rorschach Inkblot Test, the TAT, the RISB, and the C-TCB are
all forms of projective tests.
