    How would you have behaved if you were a participant in Asch’s study? Many students say they would not
     conform, that the study is outdated, and that people nowadays are more independent. To some extent this may
    be true. Research suggests that overall rates of conformity may have reduced since the time of Asch’s research.
     Furthermore, efforts to replicate Asch’s study have made it clear that many factors determine how likely it is
     that someone will demonstrate conformity to the group. These factors include the participant’s age, gender,
    and socio-cultural background (Bond & Smith, 1996; Larsen, 1990; Walker & Andrade, 1996).

