You’ve learned about many of the negative behaviors of social psychology, but the field also studies many
positive social interactions and behaviors. What makes people like each other? With whom are we friends?
Whom do we date? Researchers have documented several features of the situation that influence whether we
form relationships with others. There are also universal traits that humans find attractive in others. In this
section we discuss conditions that make forming relationships more likely, what we look for in friendships and
romantic relationships, the different types of love, and a theory explaining how our relationships are formed,
