The U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC)

The U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC) is responsible for enforcing federal laws that
make it illegal to discriminate against a job applicant or an employee because of the person''s race, color,
religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, national origin, age (40 or older), disability, or genetic
information. Figure 13.12 provides some of the legal language from laws that have been passed to prevent
discrimination.
