Increasing Happiness

Some recent findings about happiness provide an optimistic picture, suggesting that real changes in happiness
are possible. For example, thoughtfully developed well-being interventions designed to augment people’s
baseline levels of happiness may increase happiness in ways that are permanent and long-lasting, not just
temporary. These changes in happiness may be targeted at individual, organizational, and societal levels
