    Two types of therapy are psychotherapy and biomedical therapy. Both types of treatment help people with
    mental health issues, such as depression, anxiety, and schizophrenia. Psychotherapy is a psychological
     treatment that employs various methods to help someone overcome personal problems, or to attain personal
     growth. In modern practice, it has evolved into what is known as psychodynamic therapy, which will be
     discussed later. Biomedical therapy involves medication and/or medical procedures to treat psychological
     disorders. First, we will explore the various psychotherapeutic orientations outlined in Table 16.1 (many of
     these orientations were discussed in the Introduction chapter).





