The Rise of Globalization

Recent decades have seen a trend toward globalization, which is the expanding cultural, political, and
economic connections between people around the world. One measure of this is the increased buying and
selling of goods, services, and assets across national borders—in other words, international trade and financial
capital flows.

Globalization has occurred for a number of reasons. Improvements in shipping, as illustrated by the container
