Despite the rise in globalization over the last few decades, in recent years we''ve seen significant pushback
against globalization from people across the world concerned about loss of jobs, loss of political sovereignty,
and increased economic inequality. Prominent examples of this pushback include the 2016 vote in Great
Britain to exit the European Union (i.e. Brexit), and the election of Donald J. Trump for President of the United
