Figure 3.9 summarizes six factors that can shift demand curves. The direction of the arrows indicates whether
the demand curve shifts represent an increase in demand or a decrease in demand. Notice that a change in the
price of the good or service itself is not listed among the factors that can shift a demand curve. A change in the
