Figure 5.11 (a) shows inelastic demand for oil in the short run similar to that which existed for the United
States in 1973. In Figure 5.11 (a), the new equilibrium (E1) occurs at a price of $25 per barrel, roughly double
the price before the OPEC shock, and an equilibrium quantity of 16 million barrels per day. Figure 5.11 (b)
