     Decision Making by Comparing Marginal Utility
      José could use the following thought process (if he thought in utils) to make his decision regarding how many T-
        shirts and movies to purchase:

      Step 1. From Table 6.2, José can see that the marginal utility of the fourth T-shirt is 18. If José gives up the
       fourth T-shirt, then he loses 18 utils.

      Step 2. Giving up the fourth T-shirt, however, frees up $14 (the price of a T-shirt), allowing José to buy the first
      two movies (at $7 each).




