8.4 Efficiency in Perfectly Competitive Markets

Long-run equilibrium in perfectly competitive markets meets two important conditions: allocative efficiency
and productive efficiency. These two conditions have important implications. First, resources are allocated to
their best alternative use. Second, they provide the maximum satisfaction attainable by society.
