     Step 1: The Monopolist Determines Its Profit-Maximizing Level of Output

    The firm can use the points on the demand curve D to calculate total revenue, and then, based on total
     revenue, calculate its marginal revenue curve. The profit-maximizing quantity will occur where MR = MC—or at
