     competitive market, the forces of entry would erode this profit in the long run. However, a monopolist is
     protected by barriers to entry. In fact, one obvious sign of a possible monopoly is when a firm earns profits
     year after year, while doing more or less the same thing, without ever seeing increased competition eroding
     those profits.



