would operate where DL = SL, hiring Lc workers and paying Wc wage. In other words, under monopsony
employers hire fewer workers and pay a lower wage. While pure monopsony may be rare, many employers
have some degree of market power in labor markets. The outcomes for those employers will be qualitatively
similar though not as extreme as monopsony.





