Proposals for Immigration Reform

The Congressional Jordan Commission of the 1990s proposed reducing overall levels of immigration and
refocusing U.S. immigration policy to give priority to immigrants with higher skill levels. In the labor market,
focusing on high-skilled immigrants would help prevent any negative effects on low-skilled workers'' wages.
For government budgets, higher-skilled workers find jobs more quickly, earn higher wages, and pay more in
