In this chapter, we discussed the basic mechanisms of financial markets. (A more advanced course in
economics or finance will consider more sophisticated tools.) The fundamentals of those financial capital
markets remain the same: Firms are trying to raise financial capital and households are looking for a desirable
combination of rate of return, risk, and liquidity. Financial markets are society’s mechanisms for bringing
together these forces of demand and supply.
