    What does the word “investment” mean?
    What do economists mean by investment, or business spending? In calculating GDP, investment does not refer to
     purchasing stocks and bonds or trading financial assets. It refers to purchasing new capital goods, that is, new
     commercial real estate (such as buildings, factories, and stores) and equipment, residential housing construction,
    and inventories. Inventories that manufacturers produce this year are included in this year’s GDP—even if they are
     not yet sold. From the accountant’s perspective, it is as if the firm invested in its own inventories. Business
