The Power of Sustained Economic Growth

Nothing is more important for people’s standard of living than sustained economic growth. Even small
changes in the rate of growth, when sustained and compounded over long periods of time, make an enormous
difference in the standard of living. Consider Table 20.3, in which the rows of the table show several different
rates of growth in GDP per capita and the columns show different periods of time. Assume for simplicity that
an economy starts with a GDP per capita of 100. The table then applies the following formula to calculate what
GDP will be at the given growth rate in the future:


For example, an economy that starts with a GDP of 100 and grows at 3% per year will reach a GDP of 209 after
25 years; that is, 100 (1.03)25 = 209.

