This analysis helps to explain the connection that we noted earlier: that unemployment tends to rise in
recessions and to decline during expansions. The overall state of the economy shifts the labor demand curve
and, combined with wages that are sticky downwards, unemployment changes. The rise in unemployment that
occurs because of a recession is cyclical unemployment.

