Introduction to Inflation


    BRING IT HOME

A $550 Million Loaf of Bread?
If you were born within the last three decades in the United States, Canada, or many other countries in the
developed world, you probably have no real experience with a high rate of inflation. Inflation is when most prices in
an entire economy are rising. However, there is an extreme form of inflation called hyperinflation. This occurred in
Germany between 1921 and 1928, and more recently in Zimbabwe between 2008 and 2009. In November 2008,
Zimbabwe had an inflation rate of 79.6 billion percent. In contrast, in 2014, the United States had an average annual
rate of inflation of 1.6%.
