1960s and 1970s, many, especially non-economists, described its large trade surpluses either a cause or a result of
its robust economic health. However, from a standpoint of economic growth, Japan’s economy has been teetering in
and out of recession since 1990, with real GDP growth averaging only about 1% per year, and an unemployment rate
