Key Terms

balance of trade (trade balance) the gap, if any, between a nation’s exports and imports
current account balance a broad measure of the balance of trade that includes trade in goods and services, as
    well as international flows of income and foreign aid
exports of goods and services as a percentage of GDP the dollar value of exports divided by the dollar value
    of a country’s GDP
financial capital the international flows of money that facilitates trade and investment
merchandise trade balance the balance of trade looking only at goods
