    The housing bubble began to show signs of bursting in 2005, as delinquency and late payments began to grow and
     an oversupply of new homes on the market became apparent. Dropping home values contributed to a decrease in
     the overall wealth of the household sector and caused homeowners to pull back on spending. Several mortgage
