     Congressional Budget Office. Most economic recessions and upswings are times when the economy is 1–3%
    below or above potential GDP in a given year. Clearly, short-run fluctuations around potential GDP do exist, but
     over the long run, the upward trend of potential GDP determines the size of the economy.





