     have stayed out of the labor market due to early retirement, health and safety concerns, the availability of childcare,
    and school closures. As mentioned in Unemployment, these changes have caused labor force participation to
     remain lower than its historical average. The pandemic has also made it harder for future workers to acquire skills
     they need to be productive in the labor market. The longer these dynamics are at play, the more harm it will do to
      potential GDP.





