   30.3 Federal Deficits and the National Debt

    LEARNING OBJECTIVES
    By the end of this section, you will be able to:
        •  Explain the U.S. federal budget in terms of annual debt and accumulated debt
        •  Understand how economic growth or decline can influence a budget surplus or budget deficit

    Having discussed the revenue (taxes) and expense (spending) side of the budget, we now turn to the annual
     budget deficit or surplus, which is the difference between the tax revenue collected and spending over a fiscal
      year, which starts October 1 and ends September 30 of the next year.

