Summary of Fiscal Policy, Investment, and Economic Growth

Investment in physical capital, human capital, and new technology is essential for long-term economic growth,
as Table 31.2 summarizes. In a market-oriented economy, private firms will undertake most of the investment
in physical capital, and fiscal policy should seek to avoid a long series of outsized budget deficits that might
crowd out such investment. We will see the effects of many growth-oriented policies very gradually over time,
as students are better educated, we make physical capital investments, and man invents and implements new
technologies.


