Exercise D5
Explain how the multiplier works. Use an MPC of 80% in an example.

The multiplier refers to how many times a dollar will turnover in the economy. It is based on the Marginal
Propensity to Consume (MPC) which tells how much of every dollar received will be spent. If the MPC is 80%
then this means that out of every one dollar received by a consumer, $0.80 will be spent. This $0.80 is received
by another person. In turn, 80% of the $0.80 received, or $0.64, will be spent, and so on. The impact of the
multiplier is diluted when the effect of taxes and expenditure on imports is considered. To derive the
multiplier, take the 1/1 – F; where F is equal to percent of savings, taxes, and expenditures on imports.
