    apply because many high-income economies have developed economic and political institutions that
    provide a healthy economic climate for an ongoing stream of technological innovations. Continuous
    technological innovation can counterbalance diminishing returns to investments in human and physical
     capital. These two factors have the added effect of making additional technological advances even easier
     for these countries.
